{"type":"decision","classification":"foundational","recorded_at":"2026-07-20T02:15:21.234Z","evidence":{"file":"docs/PRODUCT_PLAN.md","seeds":"kicad-parts-d5f1","commit":"b0940f1d51481ae9c45074069e1749b0600a6845"},"tags":["revisions","optimistic-concurrency","audit"],"title":"Save every change to part details as a new, complete revision","rationale":"Superseded by mx-5e5fb1. At first, each details change saved a new, complete, immutable revision, grouped in a Change with a reason. Since kicad-parts-7556, a details change adds no revision; only a CAD change does. Restore was removed in kicad-parts-9296. Supplier data, stock, scans and drafts never create revisions.","id":"mx-88ce27","status":"archived","archived_at":"2026-10-13T22:34:03.977Z","archive_reason":"manual: superseded by mx-5e5fb1"}
{"type":"pattern","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-10-08T18:11:42.518Z","evidence":{"seeds":"kicad-parts-fef6","commit":"90f067a238cadc287712d35d73a96e68411001e8"},"name":"Binary-safe content addressing inside PocketBase hooks","description":"$security.sha256 hashes text, so bytes that aren't UTF-8 would hash wrongly. The CSV import sends such blobs as base64, and catalog_lib.js decodes and hashes them in pure JavaScript before storing them in the same transaction. Store documents whose SHA-256 is their identity in text fields, never json fields. Updated by mx-571a0b and mx-f11b56.","files":["infra/pocketbase/pb_hooks/catalog_lib.js","infra/pocketbase/pb_hooks/catalog_csv_imports.pb.js"],"id":"mx-be5c16","status":"archived","archived_at":"2026-10-13T22:34:04.324Z","archive_reason":"manual: superseded by mx-571a0b and mx-f11b56"}
{"type":"decision","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-10-10T05:30:01.031Z","evidence":{"seeds":"kicad-parts-9496","commit":"c4b1f70575979ad5e4ddcb9a227f95e57aee15e2"},"relates_to":["mx-0075f5"],"title":"Each CSV import run records what the CSV said","rationale":"A run's audit entry records the files read with hashes, every row's bytes, where it left each part, removed parts, and every import problem found. A run is recorded whenever its files differ from the last run, so the latest run holds what the CSV says now. tooling/catalog-import zero_loss.rs rebuilds the CSV from the latest run.","id":"mx-c5e787","supersedes":["mx-0075f5"],"status":"archived","archived_at":"2026-10-27T01:51:49.301Z","archive_reason":"manual: kicad-parts-e257 removed the CSV import, CSV reviews, import problems and the CSV overlay (ADR 0024)."}
{"type":"decision","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-10-10T05:30:05.389Z","evidence":{"seeds":"kicad-parts-23d9","commit":"c4b1f70575979ad5e4ddcb9a227f95e57aee15e2"},"relates_to":["mx-88ce27"],"title":"CSV imports state expected revisions; older checkouts and uncommitted changes are refused","rationale":"ImportCommand carries the current revision and details it expects per part, so the route answers 409 conflict or 409 newer_import_run when state moved. tooling/catalog-import refuses a checkout older than the latest import run, and uncommitted changes to the files the import reads. The overrides, allow_older_checkout and --allow-uncommitted-changes, are recorded on the audit entry.","id":"mx-64c42a","status":"archived","archived_at":"2026-10-27T01:51:49.301Z","archive_reason":"manual: kicad-parts-e257 removed the CSV import, CSV reviews, import problems and the CSV overlay (ADR 0024)."}
{"type":"pattern","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-10-10T06:58:31.732Z","evidence":{"seeds":"kicad-parts-e4ee","commit":"ca718927c732e744d321dd61d4763b9992e6cad3"},"supersedes":["mx-be5c16"],"name":"Hash CSV import blobs as UTF-8 text when possible, else in JavaScript","description":"$security.sha256 hashes text only, and passing it a Go []byte hashes '72,69,...' instead. Send UTF-8 blobs as text and store toBytes(text), about 50 ms per MiB. Send other bytes as base64, decoded and hashed in catalog_lib.js, about 3 s per MiB. The route allows 32 MiB bodies, and submit_import refuses larger ones first.","files":["infra/pocketbase/pb_hooks/catalog_csv_imports.pb.js","crates/catalog/src/pocketbase.rs","crates/catalog/src/csv_import/mod.rs"],"id":"mx-571a0b","status":"archived","archived_at":"2026-10-27T01:51:49.301Z","archive_reason":"manual: kicad-parts-e257 removed the CSV import, CSV reviews, import problems and the CSV overlay (ADR 0024)."}
{"type":"decision","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-10-10T06:59:06.682Z","evidence":{"seeds":"kicad-parts-e4ee","commit":"ca718927c732e744d321dd61d4763b9992e6cad3"},"relates_to":["mx-0075f5","mx-88ce27"],"title":"Extra MPN columns become import problems; BOM exclusion comes from KiCad flags","rationale":"Extra manufacturer part number (MPN) columns, MPN TBC and other MPN-like headers never go into part details; non-blank values become import problems. Excluded from BOM is true only when the bound local symbol says (in_bom no), or every footprint choice has exclude_from_bom. The server works it out for every new revision. zero_loss.rs checks these rules.","id":"mx-9a51aa","status":"archived","archived_at":"2026-10-27T01:51:49.301Z","archive_reason":"manual: kicad-parts-e257 removed the CSV import, CSV reviews, import problems and the CSV overlay (ADR 0024)."}
{"type":"decision","classification":"foundational","recorded_at":"2026-10-10T12:50:01.721Z","evidence":{"seeds":"kicad-parts-75a5","commit":"acc54a636ee69650eacd99daf12d231de4100ba5"},"tags":["import","edits"],"relates_to":["mx-c5e787","mx-88ce27"],"title":"App edits always win over CSV imports; accept differences field by field","rationale":"Decided 2026-10-10: a re-import never overwrites an edit. Per part and kind, details follow the CSV only while the current details came from an import, and CAD likewise; otherwise the import records a problem. When the CSV changes after an edit, the app asks the person to accept CSV values field by field (kicad-parts-75a5).","id":"mx-ee29d9","status":"archived","archived_at":"2026-10-27T01:51:49.301Z","archive_reason":"manual: kicad-parts-e257 removed the CSV import, CSV reviews, import problems and the CSV overlay (ADR 0024)."}
{"type":"decision","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-10-10T12:50:03.451Z","evidence":{"seeds":"kicad-parts-7348","commit":"acc54a636ee69650eacd99daf12d231de4100ba5"},"tags":["import","git"],"relates_to":["mx-64c42a"],"title":"Imports from uncommitted changes are refused unless overridden","rationale":"Decided 2026-10-10: commit first, because one rule is easier to explain. An import whose files differ from HEAD is refused before sending, naming the files, unless --allow-uncommitted-changes is given. The audit entry records the override. A later clean run is always recorded, so it replaces the uncommitted one. Details in mx-64c42a.","id":"mx-08bf3f","status":"archived","archived_at":"2026-10-27T01:51:49.301Z","archive_reason":"manual: kicad-parts-e257 removed the CSV import, CSV reviews, import problems and the CSV overlay (ADR 0024)."}
{"type":"pattern","classification":"foundational","recorded_at":"2026-10-11T07:48:33.362Z","evidence":{"commit":"a1b87c6","seeds":"kicad-parts-75a5"},"relates_to":["mx-ee29d9","mx-547f62","mx-404964","mx-515cef"],"name":"Reviewing CSV changes on edited parts","description":"Seed kicad-parts-75a5. POST /api/catalog/csv-reviews takes accepted field names, and the server builds what it saves from the recorded CSV document. Each review is one csv-review Change. A review covers that CSV text, so the app asks again only when the CSV changes. Problems stay recorded for the zero-loss report.","files":["infra/pocketbase/pb_migrations/1792000000_csv_reviews.js","infra/pocketbase/pb_hooks/catalog_csv_reviews.pb.js","infra/pocketbase/pb_hooks/catalog_lib.js","infra/pocketbase/pb_hooks/catalog_write_guards.pb.js","crates/catalog/src/pocketbase.rs","crates/catalog-browser/src/team.rs","apps/desktop-ui/src/team.rs","tooling/catalog-import/src/main.rs","tooling/catalog-import/tests/pocketbase_csv_reviews.rs"],"id":"mx-9bfaf5","status":"archived","archived_at":"2026-10-27T01:51:49.301Z","archive_reason":"manual: kicad-parts-e257 removed the CSV import, CSV reviews, import problems and the CSV overlay (ADR 0024)."}
{"type":"pattern","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-10-11T11:24:59.457Z","evidence":{"seeds":"kicad-parts-7828","commit":"45c5134e9284d8fbce8669128c763ab3b8647247"},"relates_to":["mx-0a590f","mx-64c42a","mx-515cef"],"name":"The import state reads only current records","description":"Seed kicad-parts-7828. read_import_state reads small fields of current records only, plus bound revisions that aren't current and the latest run per CSV file. The route accepts csvFile only as a plain name, because PocketBase filters undo only quote escapes. An index on predecessor keeps the newest-revision filter fast: 0.19 s at 6,000 revisions.","files":["crates/catalog/src/pocketbase.rs","crates/collaboration/src/client.rs","tooling/catalog-import/tests/pocketbase_import_state.rs","tooling/catalog-import/tests/pocketbase_import.rs","infra/pocketbase/pb_migrations/1792200000_cad_item_revision_successor.js","infra/pocketbase/pb_hooks/catalog_csv_imports.pb.js"],"id":"mx-e06414","status":"archived","archived_at":"2026-10-27T01:51:49.301Z","archive_reason":"manual: kicad-parts-e257 removed the CSV import, CSV reviews, import problems and the CSV overlay (ADR 0024)."}
{"type":"decision","classification":"foundational","recorded_at":"2026-10-12T05:15:04.163Z","evidence":{"seeds":"kicad-parts-3b8b","commit":"374b5cbe091a8febeec1bc020a77ca2a5f357c44"},"relates_to":["mx-ee29d9"],"title":"A CSV import never replaces CAD made in the app","rationale":"Seed kicad-parts-3b8b. A CAD item is made in the app while its current revision's Change isn't a csv-import. Imports never send such items, and bind parts to the last imported revision. If the CSV's content differs, each part using it gets csv-cad-differs-from-edited-cad-item, which a review can only keep. Storing the CSV file would replace the app's revision for KiCad.","id":"mx-4854f0","status":"archived","archived_at":"2026-10-27T01:51:49.301Z","archive_reason":"manual: kicad-parts-e257 removed the CSV import, CSV reviews, import problems and the CSV overlay (ADR 0024)."}
{"type":"decision","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-10-12T15:36:30.319Z","evidence":{"seeds":"kicad-parts-da65","commit":"57bbec8cd62f23f4abe56a4425c14a0f2729d22f"},"relates_to":["mx-e22fb9"],"title":"Library check calls made by best judgement in kicad-parts-da65","rationale":"Spec 2026-10-12 left these open; calls 1 and 8 are replaced by mx-c05d31. 'Since the last import' is per CSV file. Only errors in files the import reads stop it, with no override flag. The pilot prints the check to stderr. The desktop shows a line under the search box that opens the check in the part panel.","id":"mx-7bf4ef","status":"archived","archived_at":"2026-10-27T01:51:49.301Z","archive_reason":"manual: kicad-parts-e257 removed the CSV import, CSV reviews, import problems and the CSV overlay (ADR 0024)."}
{"type":"decision","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-10-13T15:18:48.341Z","evidence":{"seeds":"kicad-parts-da65","commit":"f104c024aa7d23ce8d27162f8d37319a4ff8369d"},"relates_to":["mx-c05d31"],"title":"Library check re-review: frozen baseline, today's CSV files, unquoted model paths","rationale":"Re-review 2026-10-13, refining mx-c05d31. The first-import exception also needs every CSV file using the footprint to be one of today's 21. The baseline is a checked-in constant in library_check/today.rs; when the fixture moves, change the test, not the list. Unquoted KiCad 5 model paths are judged too.","id":"mx-81e01f","status":"archived","archived_at":"2026-10-27T01:51:49.301Z","archive_reason":"manual: kicad-parts-e257 removed the CSV import, CSV reviews, import problems and the CSV overlay (ADR 0024)."}
{"type":"decision","title":"Add part review: revisions from our libraries count as imported","rationale":"Review 2026-10-13. A CAD item revision with source 'library' holds the CSV catalog's own file, so it's an import base, not app-made CAD. Redrawing it in KiCad and importing adds a revision with no false notice. The commit check hashes the bytes already read, so a later KiCad save can't be sent as committed.","recorded_at":"2026-10-13T16:39:57.935Z","classification":"tactical","id":"mx-aabb3a","status":"archived","archived_at":"2026-10-27T01:51:49.301Z","archive_reason":"manual: kicad-parts-e257 removed the CSV import, CSV reviews, import problems and the CSV overlay (ADR 0024)."}
{"type":"decision","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-10-17T18:22:49.437Z","evidence":{"seeds":"kicad-parts-357b","commit":"ee4d9b7e85b9ff65425383db4cf4a9e0fae10fa2"},"tags":["import","kicad-libraries","zero-loss"],"title":"Every difference from parts.sqlite needs a named rule with a reason","rationale":"csv_kicad_library/intended.rs lists the meant differences, such as supplier data left out of KiCad. Rules check values, not only columns. A difference no rule matches fails full-pilot. Fix the libraries, or add a rule with its reason; never loosen a rule to pass.","id":"mx-99d18e","status":"archived","archived_at":"2026-10-27T01:51:49.301Z","archive_reason":"manual: kicad-parts-e257 removed the CSV import, CSV reviews, import problems and the CSV overlay (ADR 0024)."}
{"type":"convention","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-10-17T19:18:42.320Z","evidence":{"seeds":"kicad-parts-357b","commit":"eb767615a6482bd14a8ab6cb2e0b83e8b5741da4"},"tags":["import","zero-loss","fixture"],"content":"parts.sqlite is frozen, so full-pilot compares the generated KiCad libraries with tables built from today's CSV files. Where the frozen copy is older, the CSV catalog fixture must record it (csv-catalog-fixture write); the rule parts-sqlite-is-older then explains it.","id":"mx-7caa23","status":"archived","archived_at":"2026-10-27T01:51:49.301Z","archive_reason":"manual: kicad-parts-e257 removed the CSV import, CSV reviews, import problems and the CSV overlay (ADR 0024)."}
{"type":"decision","classification":"foundational","recorded_at":"2026-10-18T11:05:57.357Z","evidence":{"seeds":"kicad-parts-3b72","commit":"9880bf75a811879e9a4c55f73c30d6f905dcec00"},"tags":["import","ipn"],"relates_to":["mx-ee29d9","mx-9bfaf5"],"title":"A CSV row matches an app part by MPN or exact copy","rationale":"Seed kicad-parts-3b72. A create part's CSV row that shares no MPN and is no exact copy gets ipn-given-to-another-part; the part stays. A shared MPN is trusted; N/A or TBD match nothing. The message never says they differ: the row may be the same part, so it gives both ways out.","id":"mx-45b723","status":"archived","archived_at":"2026-10-27T01:51:49.301Z","archive_reason":"manual: kicad-parts-e257 removed the CSV import, CSV reviews, import problems and the CSV overlay (ADR 0024)."}
{"type":"pattern","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-10-18T11:06:06.532Z","evidence":{"seeds":"kicad-parts-3b72","commit":"9880bf75a811879e9a4c55f73c30d6f905dcec00"},"tags":["add-part","ipn"],"relates_to":["mx-faa128"],"name":"Add part reads the CSV IPNs again; the part list does not","description":"Seed kicad-parts-3b72. catalog-browser csv_ipns.rs CsvIpns rereads database/g-*.csv when a file's size or time changes, for offering and typing an IPN. Saving calls read_fresh, and a CSV row's IPN returns IpnTaken. The part list keeps using the CSV catalog loaded at start (csv_rows_by_ipn, kicad-parts-8a71).","files":["crates/catalog-browser/src/csv_ipns.rs","crates/catalog-browser/src/lib.rs","crates/catalog-browser/src/team.rs"],"id":"mx-b1b719","status":"archived","archived_at":"2026-10-27T01:51:49.301Z","archive_reason":"manual: kicad-parts-e257 removed the CSV import, CSV reviews, import problems and the CSV overlay (ADR 0024)."}
{"type":"decision","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-10-24T05:15:34.529Z","evidence":{"seeds":"kicad-parts-8a71","commit":"8759aef58ada303c05fe8d687e5e3ea485037b06"},"relates_to":["mx-b1b719"],"title":"CSV values fill in team parts only with one team (8a71)","rationale":"Team parts keep no record of their CSV source, so who owns the CSV folder waits for kicad-parts-e9a3. Until then CSV rows fill in team parts only while one team shows parts. With two, our own rows lose it too: Source says Team catalog; the CSV table name leaves the search text. Add part counts CSV IPNs as taken.","id":"mx-2226d9","status":"archived","archived_at":"2026-10-27T01:51:49.301Z","archive_reason":"manual: kicad-parts-e257 removed the CSV import, CSV reviews, import problems and the CSV overlay (ADR 0024)."}
